me><surname>Soriano</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Cuny</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Strauss</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernardi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sequence organization and genomic distribution of the major family of interspersed repeats of mouse DNA.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1982</year><volume>79</volume><fpage>355</fpage><lpage>359</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6281768</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.79.2.355</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Soriano</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Meunier-Rotival</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernardi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The distribution of interspersed repeats is nonuniform and conserved in the mouse and human genomes.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1983</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>1816</fpage><lpage>1820</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6572942</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.80.7.1816</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Costantini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Clay</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Federico</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Saccone</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Auletta</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernardi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human chromosomal bands: nested structure, high-definition map and molecular basis.</article-title><source>Chromosoma</source><year>2006</year><volume>116</volume